---
/**
 * Web font loading for one page language (stylesheets written by scripts/build-fonts.mjs).
 * - Each language loads only its own stylesheet, without blocking render; text shows in the
 *   fallback font until it arrives (font-display: swap). jp.css carries Noto Sans JP plus
 *   the Noto Sans TC rules its characters need (TC is the fallback of the Japanese and mono
 *   stacks); tw/en load no Japanese rules.
 * - No woff2 is preloaded. Every tw first screen needs 10–13 Noto Sans TC subsets (25–80 KB
 *   each), and Chrome holds the first paint for preloaded fonts: in Lighthouse (mobile) even a
 *   single preload moved /tw/ FCP from ~2.1 s to ~5 s with no CLS gain (tw CLS is already ~0).
 *   Re-measured 2026-11-02: tc latin + tc-122 on /tw/ → FCP 2.0 → 6.5 s; on /jp/, jp latin +
 *   jp-119 (kana) removed the hero's font-swap shift (CLS 0.197 → 0) but LCP (the hero poster)
 *   went 3.3 → 4.7 s, and jp latin alone made FCP 2.7 → 4.8 s with CLS still 0.18.
 * - A per-language file, not inline @font-face: inlining (measured 2026-11-02, Lighthouse
 *   mobile) moved 18–39 KB gzip into every uncached HTML response, left the unused-CSS bytes
 *   and the /jp/ CLS unchanged, and gave no consistent FCP/LCP gain; the file is cached
 *   across pages and does not block render.
 * - B612 Mono is declared in global.css and fetched only where it renders.
 * Paths are root-relative like every other asset; scripts/pages/package.mjs rebases them.
 */
import type { Lang } from "../i18n";

interface Props { lang: Lang }
const css = `/fonts/${Astro.props.lang}.css`;
---
<link rel="preload" href={css} as="style" onload="this.onload=null;this.rel='stylesheet'" />
<noscript><link rel="stylesheet" href={css} /></noscript>
